menu "Software UART example"

config EXAMPLE_SOFTUART_RX_GPIO
    int "RX GPIO number"
    range 0 15
    default 4
    help
        GPIO that receives data (connect it to the other device's TX).
        GPIO16 cannot be used because it has no interrupt. Avoid GPIO1 and
        GPIO3 (console UART), GPIO6-11 (flash) and the boot-strapping pins
        GPIO0, GPIO2 and GPIO15. The default GPIO4 is D2 on NodeMCU boards.

config EXAMPLE_SOFTUART_TX_GPIO
    int "TX GPIO number"
    range 0 16
    default 5
    help
        GPIO that transmits data (connect it to the other device's RX).
        The default GPIO5 is D1 on NodeMCU boards.

config EXAMPLE_SOFTUART_BAUD_RATE
    int "Baud rate"
    range 300 115200
    default 9600
    help
        Line speed of the software UART. Lower rates tolerate interrupt
        latency better; 9600 baud is the best-tested rate.

config EXAMPLE_SOFTUART_INVERT
    bool "Inverted (idle-low) line logic"
    default n
    help
        Enable for devices whose serial line idles low (inverted TTL),
        for example behind a single-transistor level shifter.

endmenu
